    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4c64e38b1cccc35ea184c4a15af85921100e6dd691201a1a4dc93aa32f09ece7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof is a cross-section pipeline whose interfaces carry distinct obligations: the argument-principle/Littlewood reduction turns critical-line zero counting into a shifted mollified mean square; a uniform analytic two-shift proposition generates the differentiated mean required for that reduction; Estermann functional equations and contour deformation isolate the two symmetric main contributions; and the error analysis discards the rapidly decaying R terms before controlling the surviving E terms through dyadic decomposition and an averaged Kloosterman-sum estimate.",
